    "slug": "soso-foundation",
    "title": "The SOSO Foundation",
    "eyebrow": "About SOSO Africa",
    "summary": "True style is not measured only by what you wear,\nbut by what you give back.",
    "body": "THE SOSO FOUNDATION\n\n## We are more than fashion.\n\n01\n\nTrue style is not measured only by what you wear,\nbut by what you give back.\n\n02\nOUR PURPOSE\n\nBeyond fashion, SOSO Africa is intentional about\ngiving back to the community.\n\nWe provide food, basic necessities, and access to formal\nand informal education for those in need. We prioritize\nself-improvement and investment from in-house down to\nour individual and collective community.\n\nSOSO Africa is a vehicle for transformation, empowerment,\nand cultural elevation.\n\nFrom its inception, the business has operated with a\ncommitment to improving lives, advancing Nigeria's\ncreative economy, and preserving African identity\nthrough fashion.\n\n03 — EMPOWERMENT\n\n## Creating opportunity.\n\nSOSO Africa has empowered dozens of young Nigerians,\nespecially those from underserved backgrounds, by\nproviding access to practical training, mentorship,\nand job opportunities in the fashion industry.\n\nDOZENS\n\nOF YOUNG NIGERIANS\n\nEMPOWERED\n\n04\nSKILLS & TRAINING\n\n## Skills that become livelihoods.\n\nOur trainees are equipped with practical knowledge\nand skills that can become the foundation of sustainable\ncareers and independent businesses.\n\n01\nSewing\n\nPractical garment construction and production skills.\n\n02\nFabric Handling\n\nUnderstanding materials, quality, care, and application.\n\n03\nPattern Making\n\nDeveloping the technical foundation behind great garments.\n\n04\nFashion Business\n\nLearning the fundamentals of building and sustaining a\nfashion enterprise.\n\n05 — BUILDING INDEPENDENCE\n\n## From learning to launching.\n\nHigh-performing students are offered employment within\nSOSO Africa or supported in launching their own fashion\nstartups.\n\nThe company also provides starter kits — including\nsewing machines, fabrics, and tools — to select graduates\nto help them become economically self-reliant.\n\nTRAIN\nTeach practical skills.\n\nMENTOR\nBuild confidence and capability.\n\nEMPOWER\nCreate pathways to independence.\n\n06 — BEYOND BUSINESS\n\n## Fashion as a force for development.\n\nThese actions directly align with Nigeria's national\ngoals of job creation, youth development, and economic\ndiversification.\n\nSOSO Africa has gone beyond its business boundaries\nto touch lives through education-based CSR programs.\n\n07\nEDUCATION AS IMPACT\n\n## Sometimes empowerment begins with a chance.\n\nSOSO Africa has supported students in low-income\ncommunities who were unable to afford examination fees,\nhelping remove a barrier between young people and\ntheir education.\n\nEDUCATION SUPPORT\n\nWASSCE / WAEC\n\n& NECO\n\nRegistration fees sponsored for students\nin low-income communities.\n\n08 — THE FULL CIRCLE\n\n## Education. Skill. Opportunity.\n\nSome of the students supported through education later\nenrolled in SOSO Africa's fashion training programmes.\n\nA number of them have gone on to start their own\nbusinesses, while others have joined the company's\nworkforce.\n\nEDUCATION\n\nTRAINING\n\nEMPLOYMENT\n\nINDEPENDENCE\n\n09 — CULTURAL PRESERVATION\n\n## Every stitch tells a story.\n\nAt its core, SOSO Africa's work preserves and promotes\nAfrican identity.\n\nThrough its designs, fabric choices, embroidery, and\nstylistic expressions, the brand retells African stories\nin every stitch.\n\n10\nCULTURAL CONTRIBUTIONS\n\n01\n\n## Afrocentric Aesthetics\n\nDesigns that reflect local heritage and indigenous\nexpressions.\n\n02\n\n## Traditional Fabrics\n\nAnkara, Aso Oke, cotton blends, and other traditional\nfabrics reimagined for modern fashion.\n\n03\n\n## African Visibility\n\nPromoting African fashion locally and internationally\nthrough online visibility, international clientele,\nand Pan-African engagement.\n\nSOSO AFRICA\n\n## More than fashion.\n\nSOSO Africa is actively contributing to the intellectual\nand economic value of African creativity.\n\nTRANSFORMATION · EMPOWERMENT · CULTURAL ELEVATION",
    "sourceUrl": "https://shopsoso.co/about-soso-the-soso-foundation/",
